      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The desire to have a say in something that truly belongs to you is a very human and powerful yearning, especially when everything feels controlled. Even if the external world remains fixed, your internal reaction to it is an area where you have absolute sovereignty. You can choose how you interpret the monotony, how you respond to the pressure, or what moments you choose to truly *feel* rather than just *process*. That internal resistance, that private act of refusal, is the most authentic thing you have.",
      "source": "target",
